      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should the initial value be 1 and limit 1 instead (a binary semaphore that\u0027s initially available)? It seems like we only care whether there\u0027s been an event that the thread hasn\u0027t seen yet, so letting it run two iterations before blocking doesn\u0027t seem useful.\n\nIf using a binary semaphore then a poll signal could be used, which the documentation seems to suggest is somewhat cheaper to use.",
