      "writtenOn": "2022-05-06T01:10:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It seems like most states will stay where they are if no signals change, and a relatively small minority want to move to some other state on a delay. Rather than making this code poll those cases (for instance, S5 inactivity timeout), could those instead set timers that unblock this loop so all processing is event-driven?\n\nIt looks like there are only three situations where the state machine should run a turn:\n* a signal value changed: interrupt wakes this thread\n* a timer expired: can wake this thread from a timer expiration function\n* the state machine transitioned to a new state, which should run immediately\n\nThese can all be expressed with relative ease I think, and avoid ever needing to poll state from this thread.",
      "revId": "82e18ff6162defc8f2d2f8cd9aa34e95afa10b07",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
